REFUTATION: the convergent n/Phi_6 is NOT the covering-min for n>=7.

n=7: [1, 2, 5, 6, 7, 8]
   M = 2/13 = 0.153846  at t=4/13   (grid-max 0.153845 -> no underestimate: True)
   construction n/Phi_6 = 7/43 = 0.162791   ==> beats construction: True
   valid covering (n-1)-set (covers 2..n, primitive, size n-1): True;  M>1/n: True
n=8: [1, 4, 5, 6, 7, 11, 16]
   M = 2/15 = 0.133333  at t=8/15   (grid-max 0.133332 -> no underestimate: True)
   construction n/Phi_6 = 8/57 = 0.140351   ==> beats construction: True
   valid covering (n-1)-set (covers 2..n, primitive, size n-1): True;  M>1/n: True
n=9: [1, 3, 4, 5, 7, 11, 18, 32]
   M = 4/33 = 0.121212  at t=29/33   (grid-max 0.121212 -> no underestimate: True)
   construction n/Phi_6 = 9/73 = 0.123288   ==> beats construction: True
   valid covering (n-1)-set (covers 2..n, primitive, size n-1): True;  M>1/n: True

CONCLUSION: there is no mediant->convergent transition at n=7; the convergent is NOT the
covering-min. LRC floor untouched (all M>1/n). See HYP-3725, MISTAKE-087, CASE-convergent-not-covering-min.
